\n\n(Studio: Brian Williams) Statement from Governor Sarah Palin about being in national politics to stay and tomorrow\u2019s interview with Obama noted. ", "segment_duration": 330, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63060.0", "legacy_segment_id": 922203, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "iFj7uYe0wN", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-29", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 922202, "segment_id": "wWV1UA4TfS", "segment_broadcast_id": "iFj7uYe0wN", "segment_title": "Making Your Vote Count (Voter Suppression)", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.   (New York: Rehema Ellis) Rumors and misinformation aimed at holding down voter turnout examined; scenes shown of early voters; details given about a flyer in Virginia with a false date for Democrats to vote and questions involving foreclosure, wearing campaign items, students changing address, acceptable identification and outstanding parking tickets. [New VOTER \u2013 comments.] [Election Protection Jonah GOLDMAN&#134;- says new voters are more vulnerable to misinformation; debunks the myths.]   (Studio: Brian Williams) Information on where to turn with voting questions presented. ", "segment_duration": 160, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63390.0", "legacy_segment_id": 922204, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "iFj7uYe0wN", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-29", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network":